  "$comment": "Threads (Phase 4, P4.2). The seed connections from docs/PLAN.md §14 as OSIS references in WEBC (English) numbering, each with an original explanation and its citations: OpenBible.info cross-reference rows, words the WEBC text itself carries at a verse (checked at build), shared Greek words at their Septuagint and TAGNT rows (checked by `pnpm connections:verify`), and, for every interpretive reading, a Church Father's work and section in a pinned public-domain edition with a phrase that must occur there. Where the plan names several passages, each is its own connection; the plan's 'Exodus (whole)' is anchored at Exod 19:1, where the Septuagint uses the word Luke 9:31 shares, and 'Genesis–Kings' at Abraham's call through the temple's dedication. A connection is shown on the site only once it is `verified`, with the owner's approval carrying a fingerprint of its content.",
