    {
      "id": "s11a",
      "from": "Exod.12",
      "to": "Luke.22.7-Luke.22.20",
      "type": "typology",
      "strength": 3,
      "label": "Passover at the Last Supper",
      "explanation": "Luke sets the Last Supper on the day the Passover lamb was sacrificed, and Jesus tells the twelve he has longed to eat this Passover with them before he suffers. Exodus 12 commands the lamb, its blood on the doorposts and a meal kept as a memorial through the generations; at the supper Jesus gives the bread and tells them to do this in memory of him. Tertullian notes that of all the feasts Jesus chose the Passover for his suffering, and Chrysostom says that where the type was, Christ set the truth.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "kind": "xref",
          "row": "OpenBibleXref:L261348"
        },
        {
          "kind": "xref",
